# Trailmaster X2

A pocket quick-start guide. Keep this leaflet with the device — it folds
flat into the carry pouch.

The Trailmaster X2 is a handheld field logger. This guide covers the
first charge, the four-button interface, and day-to-day care. For the
full manual and firmware updates, see the support section on the back.

## In the box

- Trailmaster X2 unit
- USB-C charging cable (1 m)
- Wrist lanyard
- This leaflet

If anything is missing, do not power the unit on — contact support
before first use so the warranty window is preserved.

## First run

1. **Charge fully.** Connect the USB-C cable to any 5 V source. The ring
   light pulses amber while charging and holds green when full (about two
   hours from empty).
2. **Power on.** Hold the **Power** button for three seconds until the
   ring light flashes once.
3. **Set the clock.** On first boot the unit asks for the date and time.
   Use **Up** / **Down** to change a field and **Select** to advance.
4. **Start logging.** A short press of **Select** from the home screen
   begins a new track. The ring light blinks green once per sample.

> Tip: a double-press of **Power** at any time toggles the backlight
> without interrupting an active log.

## Button reference

| Button | Short press | Long press (3 s) |
|--------|-------------|------------------|
| Power  | Backlight   | On / off         |
| Up     | Previous    | Jump to top      |
| Down   | Next        | Jump to bottom   |
| Select | Start / mark| Open menu        |

## Care and safety

{% callout type="warning" %}
The X2 is splash-resistant, not submersible. Do not rinse it under a tap
or leave it in standing water. Wipe the contacts dry before charging.
{% /callout %}

- Operating range: −10 °C to 45 °C.
- Charge at least once every three months when in storage.
- The battery is not user-replaceable; return the unit for servicing.

A unit that has been fully discharged for a long period may need a few
minutes on the cable before the ring light responds. This is normal.

## Support

- Manual and firmware: visit the support portal and search for "X2".
- Warranty: 24 months from purchase, parts and labour.
- Lost this leaflet? A printable copy is on the portal.

Thank you for choosing Trailmaster. Pack light, log everything.
